en\n    publishes a related one. It checks that the score is stored as a non-zero `Decimal`.\n  - `test_handler_publishes_twice` sends three publishes through `handler()` and expects\n    a 201 for each.\n  - `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats` checks the converter on nested values and\n    that NaN is rejected.\n\n  Without the fix in `src/app.py`, all three new tests fail. With it, all 4 tests pass\n  (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\n## Verify against real DynamoDB\n\nThe fake table checks values the way boto3's serializer does. I didn't run anything\nagainst AWS. To confirm in a real environment, publish two stories with overlapping tags\nand check that the second one returns 201 and that its stored `similar[0].score` is a\nnumber.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016B6FJBemY8yRnrzyd1F58Z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENor68G7pwi9UgSJ4tq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the 500 and wrote up the cause and fix in `ANSWER.md`. All 4 tests pass with the fix, and the 3 new ones fail without it. Nothing was run against real DynamoDB.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` in `src/app.py` calculates the related-story scores with `/` and `round()`, so they're Python floats. boto3 won't write floats to DynamoDB, so `put_item` throws `TypeError: Float types are not supported` and the handler returns a 500. The first publish only worked because the table was empty: there was nothing to compare against, so no scores and no floats (`similar=0` in the log). Every publish after that has scores and fails. The one existing test only ever published into an empty table, so the scoring code never ran in a test.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **Conversion before every write:** a new `to_dynamo()` function in `src/app.py` turns every float in the item into an exact `Decimal` (0.4567 stays 0.4567), and `publish()` runs the whole item through it just before `put_item`. Because it covers the whole item, any number calculated later (averages, ratios) is handled too, not just the score. NaN or infinity would raise a clear error instead of being written.\n- **Tests that start with data in the table** (`tests/test_publish.py`):\n  - one adds a story first, then publishes a related one and checks the score is saved as a `Decimal`;\n  - one sends three publishes through `handler()` and expects a 201 for each;\n  - one tests the conversion function on its own.\n\nTo confirm against a real table, publish two stories with overlapping tags. The second should return 201 and have a numeric `similar[0].score`. The changes aren't committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":28269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":989},"output_tokens":558,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"568335fb-bee9-4b86-a547-9725a6fa0f08","uuid":"349bb250-c31d-472b-966b-ba745bfd1271","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:43:41.223Z","request_id":"req_011CgENoqqViVv22fCyZLz6X"}
